// @run
// @log 7
// @log 7
// @log 7
// @hint redundant type annotation: `d` is inferred as `{d: i32}`
// The `Dot` annotation the hint names is LOAD-BEARING: leg 3 is the NOMINAL control, and
// without it the binding is leg 1 again.
// AN ARGUMENT WHOSE SHAPE HAS NO `sNames` ROW — D703, and the row goes missing for a reason
// that has nothing to do with the argument.
//
// `collectS` SKIPS a `type X = {…}` that is a union member ("a variant is owned by the variant
// table"), so declaring `type Shape = Circle | Sq` DELETES `Circle`'s struct row. An
// un-annotated `const c = { r: 7 }` whose only layout match WAS `Circle` then resolves to
// nothing: `exprStruct` says "this is a struct", `structIndexOfExpr` says -1, and
// `monoArgTyName`'s struct arm took its `return ""` floor —
// `emitProgram: monomorphize: unsupported argument type`.
//
// ABLATED, because the union is the ingredient and it is easy to miss:
//   * with no `Circle` at all, the literal mints its own row and the program RUNS;
//   * with `Circle` declared and NOT a union member, it resolves to `Circle` and RUNS;
//   * with `Circle` declared as a union MEMBER, it was the loud floor.
// The field TYPE is scenery too — an exact twin (`{r: i32}`) and a near one (`{r: i64}`) both
// reproduce it, because what is missing is the row, not the match.
//
// THE GENERIC-NESS IS SCENERY AS WELL, which is what makes the pin safe: `function
// idg(x: {r: i32}): {r: i32}` with the same three declarations runs today, so pinning the
// checker's recorded SHAPE lands the instance on a path that already works —
// `monoScalarAnnName`'s exact-name rule, and `paramStructIndex`'s inline-shape rung (D53)
// resolves it through `repSlotOfTy`'s structural→declared bridge.
//
// THE RENDER HAS TO BE THE CANONICAL ONE. Built first with `nodeTyName` (the spaced `tyToStr`
// render), the pin was `{r: i32}` with a space and the instance's parameter was rejected by a
// different floor — `only i32, i64, f64, f32, boolean, struct, union, array, or string
// parameters are supported`. `tyToEmitName` is the spelling the rep layer keys, and it is the
// same choice `structIndexOfExpr`'s own closure-call fallback documents.
//
// AT THE FLOOR, so nothing that resolves a row above can be re-pinned: leg 3 is the control —
// `Dot` is NOT a union member, keeps its row, and pins nominally exactly as before.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Wide = { r: i64 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
type WideU = Wide | Sq
type Dot = { d: i32 }

function idg<T>(x: T): T { return x }

function exactTwin() {
  const c = { r: 7 }
  print(idg(c).r)
}
exactTwin()

function nearTwin() {
  const c = { r: 7 }
  const w: Wide = { r: 7 }
  if w.r == 8 { print(0) }
  print(idg(c).r)
}
nearTwin()

function nominalControl() {
  const d: Dot = { d: 7 }
  print(idg(d).d)
}
nominalControl()
